# Sample size for a matched case-control study, an invented example: correlation 0.2, 30% of controls exposed, odds ratio 2, 3 controls per case, power 80%, alpha 5%; then the paired design. One fragment per line.
case-control correlation = 0.2
probability of exposure in controls = 0.3
odds ratio = 2
controls per case subject = 3
alpha = 0.05
power = 0.8
Estimated minimum sample size (cases required) = 108
Reduction in sample size, relative to paired design,
when using 3 controls per case = 0.6
controls per case subject = 1
Estimated minimum sample size (cases required) = 180
